# Lobster/OpenClaw Workflows for Multi-Repo Work

RULE: For systematic improvements across all 30+ repos, use lobster workflows instead of ad-hoc parallel agents.
WHY: Lobster workflows are rules-driven (read from .cursorrules + .mdc files automatically), verify completeness against codex specs, and handle 30+ repos in 6 parallel workers.
CODEX: 06-coding-standards/sub-agent-workflow.md

Available workflows:
  lobster run .lobster/harden-all-repos.lobster      # Pass quality gates (~60 min)
  lobster run .lobster/improve-test-coverage.lobster  # Reach 50% coverage (~90 min)
  lobster run .lobster/complete-ai-epic-tasks.lobster # Complete AI-doable epics (~2-3 hrs)

Task scope:
  AI-doable (Harsh-owned): 591 tasks
  Human-required (Ikenna-owned): 161 tasks  ← lobster skips these
  Unknown: 647 tasks

Key features:
  Rules-driven — reads .cursorrules + .mdc files, no hardcoding
  Completeness-verified — checks epics/ "definition of done"
  Test quality — expands existing files, no test_*_extended.py
  AI/Human separation — skips D6/D7 blockers, manual validation tasks

See: .lobster/FOR_AGENTS.md for quick start, .lobster/README.md for full docs
